# Logging and Observability

Use structured logs, not `print()`.

Every call-related log should include where available: `call_id`, `room_name`, `participant_identity`, `session_id`, `tool_name`, `provider`, `duration_ms`, `status`, `error_code`.

Track: connection time, first response latency, speech-to-speech latency, tool-call latency, interruption count, model/SIP errors, call duration, disconnect reason, task completion, human handoff rate.

Never log: API keys, access tokens, full payment details, passwords, sensitive PII, complete raw audio, or unredacted confidential transcripts.
